// Ch8 B11 "The hoist" (act1_ch08.md §2 B11; W12). In-engine, between Wave 1 and Wave 2: the spawn have
// pulled back down the wall face in a lull of the surge. Liss looks at the stair, at the crowd, and at
// two Watchers on the parapet with their stone mouths open. She drives iron pins into the Watchers'
// mouths, hangs her blocks off them and runs a rope down the wall's inner face beside the stair, with a
// fish-basket on the end. PLAIN ROPE AND IRON, nothing bound (ADR 0017 (c); rule 1).
// Liss's tell in reverse: working means she's fine. The first basket comes up with three children in
// it. Toma looks at the pins in the Watchers' mouths, then takes the rope's tail and hauls without a
// word (his devotion is to the people; the Order's view of the stone comes in B18).
// Sets ch08_hoist_rigged (Liss's Haul, skills.json hoist_haul requires_flag).
title: ch08_hoist
location: ch08/corrow
---
@camera W12
@music seawall_hold
@mark liss hoist_liss walk
@anim liss look_at watchers_mouths
@wait 1.0
@anim liss drive_pin watchers_mouths
@sfx watchers_pin
Stillguard [angry]: Those are the Watchers! #line:ch08_hoist_001
Ivo [determined]: Children first. Argue with the stone after. #line:ch08_hoist_002
@sfx watchers_pin
@sfx hoist_block
Liss [determined]: Seat the pin. Seat it. She'll hold. #line:ch08_hoist_003
<<set $ch08_hoist_rigged = true>>
@anim liss haul_rope
@sfx hoist_block
@wait 2.0
@mark child_a basket_top_a walk
@mark child_b basket_top_b walk
@mark child_c basket_top_c walk
@wait 1.0
@anim toma look_at watchers_mouths
@wait 1.0
@mark toma hoist_toma walk via=way_approach_east,way_approach_foot
@anim toma haul_rope
@wait 1.0
===
